259
00:18:39,480 --> 00:18:42,160
Like certain adults around here.
Not good, not good.

260
00:18:42,599 --> 00:18:45,680
Come on want to go slide the worm? Woooo.

261
00:18:51,359 --> 00:18:53,839
That’s just how Rapee is.

262
00:18:54,279 --> 00:18:57,359
He’s had a bad mouth since he was little.
Please don’t take it to heart.

263
00:18:57,640 --> 00:19:00,239
P’Pee said he wanted
to introduce me to his close friend.

264
00:19:00,240 --> 00:19:01,839
Is there something you wanted?

265
00:19:02,400 --> 00:19:07,799
Well... earlier, Pee came to me
because he said something harsh to you.

266
00:19:08,079 --> 00:19:10,880
He wants to make it up to you,
but he doesn’t know how.

267
00:19:11,839 --> 00:19:14,719
Has P’Pee really never had
to make up with anyone before?

268
00:19:14,720 --> 00:19:18,240
Pee is... how should I put it...

269
00:19:18,559 --> 00:19:22,118
driven. So he’s not very social.

270
00:19:22,119 --> 00:19:23,680
He doesn’t really have friends.

271
00:19:24,839 --> 00:19:26,440
It’s not that bad.

272
00:19:26,599 --> 00:19:30,920
He just works all the time,
so he never lets himself drift

273
00:19:31,079 --> 00:19:33,759
I used to be a lot like Pee too

274
00:19:33,920 --> 00:19:36,759
I was serious about studying,
so that’s how we got close.

275
00:19:37,480 --> 00:19:41,119
But when I got pregnant,
the father wouldn’t take responsibility.

276
00:19:41,319 --> 00:19:43,879
So Pee stepped in and helped.

277
00:19:43,880 --> 00:19:46,239
He’s cared for Ryan like his own son.

278
00:19:46,240 --> 00:19:48,880
He really is a very good person.

279
00:19:49,160 --> 00:19:51,440
- Wooo.
- Wooo.

280
00:19:51,920 --> 00:19:52,920
How was it, Un?

281
00:19:53,160 --> 00:19:55,080
- Did sliding the worm clear things up?
- It did.

282
00:19:55,119 --> 00:19:57,640
But what would sliding the dog be like?

283
00:19:58,279 --> 00:19:59,920
Ryan.

284
00:20:03,640 --> 00:20:06,640
Guys, get ready to practice. I’m almost back.

285
00:20:13,480 --> 00:20:15,240
Hey, P’Pee.

286
00:20:18,119 --> 00:20:19,240
Kao.

287
00:20:19,640 --> 00:20:20,559
Where are you going, P’Pee?

288
00:20:20,560 --> 00:20:21,798
That’s the way to my room.

289
00:20:21,799 --> 00:20:22,920
I’m going to your room.

290
00:20:23,119 --> 00:20:25,079
- There’s a centipede under my foot!
- Hey, where?

291
00:20:25,160 --> 00:20:27,000
Kao, where is it? Shit.

292
00:20:27,279 --> 00:20:28,519
Left foot, left foot.

293
00:20:29,160 --> 00:20:31,880
Code red. Evacuate now.

294
00:20:32,039 --> 00:20:34,079
Hey, shit she’s lying.

295
00:20:35,359 --> 00:20:37,240
P’Pee, Kao said it’s not a good time.

296
00:20:37,799 --> 00:20:40,160
- Then let’s just go in together.
- P’Pee!!

297
00:20:44,480 --> 00:20:48,279
Oh, hello, Mr. Rapee. Ms. Noppakao.

298
00:20:48,839 --> 00:20:50,039
Uh...

299
00:20:51,759 --> 00:20:54,759
Hello.

300
00:20:55,119 --> 00:20:56,359
I’m Gunya.

301
00:20:56,720 --> 00:20:57,720
Huh?

302
00:20:58,759 --> 00:21:00,319
Why are you saying your real name?

303
00:21:04,480 --> 00:21:07,200
I didn’t want to tell you this, P’Pee...

304
00:21:08,599 --> 00:21:10,000
but I might as well.

305
00:21:10,480 --> 00:21:11,480
What?

306
00:21:12,079 --> 00:21:13,079
Well...

307
00:21:13,200 --> 00:21:15,400
Kao’s been secretly renting
the room out during the day.

308
00:21:15,599 --> 00:21:17,719
Then where do you sleep? I don’t see a bed.

309
00:21:17,720 --> 00:21:21,799
Right here. Gun goes home in the evening.

310
00:21:22,039 --> 00:21:23,839
Huh. On the couch?

311
00:21:25,640 --> 00:21:28,078
P’Pee, I really needed money.

312
00:21:28,079 --> 00:21:30,518
Needed money for what? I already gave you a lot.

313
00:21:30,519 --> 00:21:32,240
What did you do with it? This room?

314
00:21:35,680 --> 00:21:37,758
Just wait. I’m gonna blast them to pieces.

315
00:21:37,759 --> 00:21:39,798
- Wow, you talk big, asshole.
- Hey, what’s this?

316
00:21:39,799 --> 00:21:41,598
- Hello.
- Hello.

317
00:21:41,599 --> 00:21:43,479
- Who’s this?
- Hello, Mr. Phosathon.

318
00:21:43,480 --> 00:21:45,038
Hello, Nong Pete.

319
00:21:45,039 --> 00:21:46,758
Did you forget something?

320
00:21:46,759 --> 00:21:49,440
- Forgot something.
- Why are you talking all polite, bro?

321
00:21:52,119 --> 00:21:55,559
Oh, right, right. Yeah, we forgot something.

322
00:21:55,799 --> 00:21:58,239
Excuse us, let me go grab it first.

323
00:21:58,240 --> 00:21:59,598
- Of course. Go right ahead.
- What the hell did we forget?

324
00:21:59,599 --> 00:22:01,559
- Just grab something.
- Okay.

325
00:22:04,720 --> 00:22:06,720
Did you forget your figure? Your figure?

326
00:22:18,079 --> 00:22:19,640
Nice to meet you, handsome.

327
00:22:21,119 --> 00:22:22,119
Hey.

328
00:22:22,400 --> 00:22:23,480
My gun.

329
00:22:25,799 --> 00:22:26,880
Mm.

330
00:22:43,759 --> 00:22:46,000
Come talk to me outside. Now.

331
00:22:48,759 --> 00:22:49,880
What are you doing, huh?

332
00:22:50,359 --> 00:22:51,799
What are you doing, huh?

333
00:22:52,519 --> 00:22:54,559
- Kao rents the room out during the day.
- What?

334
00:22:55,400 --> 00:22:56,839
- Yeah.
- Renting it out.

335
00:22:57,160 --> 00:22:58,838
And there are all these people here too?
People I don’t even know?

336
00:22:58,839 --> 00:23:00,319
- People I don’t even know?
- What?

337
00:23:00,839 --> 00:23:01,839
I mean...

338
00:23:02,119 --> 00:23:03,079
what I’m saying is,

339
00:23:03,080 --> 00:23:04,880
with all these people around, it’s dangerous.

340
00:23:05,119 --> 00:23:08,079
Why don’t you sleep in my room for now? It’s safer.

341
00:23:08,759 --> 00:23:11,240
You don’t have to worry,
P’PeeThey’re all Kao’s friends.

342
00:23:11,400 --> 00:23:12,799
So relax.

343
00:23:14,440 --> 00:23:15,440
What?

344
00:23:22,079 --> 00:23:23,160
Rejected again.

345
00:23:45,359 --> 00:23:48,200
Easy, easy. Slow down.

346
00:23:48,359 --> 00:23:50,200
Pray.

347
00:24:00,079 --> 00:24:01,079
Uh...

348
00:24:03,359 --> 00:24:05,680
I...

349
00:24:06,799 --> 00:24:07,799
I...

350
00:24:08,599 --> 00:24:10,119
I...

351
00:24:12,359 --> 00:24:13,680
Let’s go.

352
00:24:14,599 --> 00:24:15,680
Go.

353
00:24:16,359 --> 00:24:17,519
Go.

354
00:24:18,240 --> 00:24:19,480
Go where?

355
00:24:21,000 --> 00:24:22,359
Let’s go eat.

356
00:24:24,400 --> 00:24:25,400
Go eat?

357
00:24:32,319 --> 00:24:34,160
You said you were taking me to dinner.

358
00:24:34,759 --> 00:24:36,960
Well, I brought you to eat something you like.

359
00:24:43,079 --> 00:24:44,079
What?

360
00:24:44,400 --> 00:24:45,519
Since when?

361
00:24:46,119 --> 00:24:47,160
Damn, this is good.

362
00:24:47,359 --> 00:24:48,920
This is really good, P’Pee.

363
00:24:49,519 --> 00:24:50,839
- P’Pee.
- Hm?

364
00:24:53,839 --> 00:24:55,240
See? It’s good, right?

365
00:24:55,359 --> 00:24:56,680
Uh...

366
00:25:02,160 --> 00:25:04,160
- Yeah, it’s good, right?
- It really is.

367
00:25:04,720 --> 00:25:06,480
I heard Kao likes this.

368
00:25:06,759 --> 00:25:08,039
Likes it since when?

369
00:25:08,200 --> 00:25:10,919
Back when we were kids. Whenever Kao came
to ask P’Pee and P’Phat to play basketball,

370
00:25:10,920 --> 00:25:13,720
you always ended up
eating frog with us. I didn’t like it.

371
00:25:14,160 --> 00:25:19,680
Back then I only ate it
because P’Phat made me.

372
00:25:29,640 --> 00:25:31,159
- Uh, P’Pee.
- Hm?

373
00:25:31,160 --> 00:25:33,439
Kao remembers that when we were kids,

374
00:25:33,440 --> 00:25:36,279
you wanted to be on the national basketball team, right?

375
00:25:36,559 --> 00:25:38,720
So why did you stop playing?

376
00:25:40,240 --> 00:25:42,400
Mm...

377
00:25:45,079 --> 00:25:46,758
Well...

378
00:25:46,759 --> 00:25:48,599
I messed up just now.

379
00:25:52,200 --> 00:25:56,319
See? I told you, you messed up. Got it?

380
00:25:58,200 --> 00:25:59,960
- What?
- Can I have one more try?

381
00:26:01,960 --> 00:26:03,680
- Let’s go.
- Hm?

382
00:26:04,039 --> 00:26:06,335
- Where are you going, Kao?
- P’Pee, hurry up and follow me.

383
00:26:06,359 --> 00:26:07,720
Come on.

384
00:26:08,480 --> 00:26:10,318
Kids, are you hungry?

385
00:26:10,319 --> 00:26:11,839
- Yes!
- Yes!

386
00:26:22,880 --> 00:26:24,200
Layup.

387
00:26:31,920 --> 00:26:34,480
Just kidding. I was trying to make you laugh.

388
00:26:35,480 --> 00:26:37,119
Look Jordan.

389
00:26:38,319 --> 00:26:39,599
Hey, look.

390
00:26:40,720 --> 00:26:41,839
Hey.

391
00:26:48,039 --> 00:26:49,039
Come on.

392
00:26:49,279 --> 00:26:50,799
- Not taking it?
- What are you doing?

393
00:26:50,960 --> 00:26:52,640
Didn’t you want to be a basketball player?

394
00:26:54,200 --> 00:26:55,200
Sigh...

395
00:26:55,839 --> 00:26:58,640
I was trying to jog your memory.

396
00:27:00,039 --> 00:27:03,440
Whoa...

397
00:27:04,200 --> 00:27:05,279
That’s called a layup.

398
00:27:11,319 --> 00:27:12,000
Jordan.

399
00:27:12,001 --> 00:27:13,400
Come on.

400
00:27:13,559 --> 00:27:14,559
- Come on, Kao.
- Hey.

401
00:27:15,359 --> 00:27:16,359
P’Pee.

402
00:27:18,599 --> 00:27:20,200
Hey... give me that.

403
00:27:31,160 --> 00:27:32,839
Mm That’s so cute, isn’t it?

404
00:27:33,000 --> 00:27:34,440
Yeah. Cute.

405
00:27:56,920 --> 00:27:58,799
- Dig for shrimp paste.
- Hey, hey, hey.

406
00:28:03,200 --> 00:28:06,959
- Come on, hurr.
- Dig for shrimp paste.

407
00:28:06,960 --> 00:28:10,440
- Yay.
- Yay.

408
00:28:13,240 --> 00:28:15,838
It’s in! It’s in.

409
00:28:15,839 --> 00:28:17,279
Nice one, Kao.

410
00:28:17,799 --> 00:28:19,000
The teacher is pretty awesome.

411
00:28:21,400 --> 00:28:22,720
Does this hurt?

412
00:28:22,960 --> 00:28:24,279
A little.

413
00:28:27,799 --> 00:28:29,200
- P’Pee.
- Hm?

414
00:28:29,720 --> 00:28:32,799
You’re so good at basketball.

415
00:28:33,480 --> 00:28:35,039
Why did you give it up?

416
00:28:35,359 --> 00:28:36,880
Don’t you miss it?

417
00:28:38,319 --> 00:28:40,160
Mm.

418
00:28:40,759 --> 00:28:42,119
Not really.

419
00:28:43,519 --> 00:28:45,079
There were more important things.

420
00:28:48,680 --> 00:28:50,000
I feel bad for you, then.

421
00:28:50,440 --> 00:28:52,079
Why?

422
00:28:53,680 --> 00:28:55,960
Was it because of P’Phankorn?

423
00:28:57,759 --> 00:29:00,680
I forgot you and P’Phan used to be close.

424
00:29:04,039 --> 00:29:05,240
But...

425
00:29:06,359 --> 00:29:10,519
after P’Phan ran away from home, Dad died too.

426
00:29:12,759 --> 00:29:14,799
So it was just Mom and me left.

427
00:29:15,839 --> 00:29:18,119
That’s why I had to take over the hotel.

428
00:29:21,160 --> 00:29:24,759
But you’re happy, right, P’Pee?

429
00:29:25,079 --> 00:29:26,680
Well, I have to be.

430
00:29:26,880 --> 00:29:29,839
If I wasn’t, why would I do it? Right?

431
00:29:31,799 --> 00:29:32,799
Mm.

432
00:29:39,839 --> 00:29:42,039
Dreams and reality...

433
00:29:42,519 --> 00:29:44,240
they’re really not the same, huh?

434
00:30:10,519 --> 00:30:11,519
Hm?

435
00:30:14,640 --> 00:30:15,640
What?

436
00:30:16,119 --> 00:30:17,640
- P’Pee.
- Hm?

437
00:30:17,920 --> 00:30:19,799
Look at this do you remember?

438
00:30:24,079 --> 00:30:25,079
Hey.

439
00:30:28,960 --> 00:30:30,039
- P’Pee.
- Hm?

440
00:30:30,200 --> 00:30:31,200
Look at this.

441
00:30:31,799 --> 00:30:33,279
Why the hell are you pulling that?

442
00:30:33,720 --> 00:30:34,720
Was that a curse?

443
00:30:35,160 --> 00:30:36,960
I wasn’t cursing. Let me see what’s there.

444
00:30:37,640 --> 00:30:38,920
Hey.

445
00:30:40,200 --> 00:30:42,078
Shit. It’s like a time machine.

446
00:30:42,079 --> 00:30:45,200
Back when we were kids, you were such a scribbler, P’Pee.

447
00:30:46,000 --> 00:30:47,719
Who wrote this? Pinocchio?

448
00:30:47,720 --> 00:30:49,599
Pi-no-cc-hio.

449
00:30:50,039 --> 00:30:52,079
P’Pee. Yours?

450
00:30:52,319 --> 00:30:54,079
Whose else would it be? You, huh?

451
00:31:25,079 --> 00:31:26,079
Sorry.

452
00:31:29,000 --> 00:31:31,200
Let me take this call.

453
00:31:34,400 --> 00:31:35,440
Hello, Rung?

454
00:31:42,599 --> 00:31:43,640
What?

455
00:31:45,960 --> 00:31:47,839
Okay, okay. I’ll head over now.

456
00:31:49,799 --> 00:31:51,000
Sigh...

457
00:31:53,119 --> 00:31:54,480
Mm. Okay.

458
00:31:57,519 --> 00:32:00,400
Kao, Ryan’s gone missing. I’ve got to go first.

459
00:32:01,559 --> 00:32:03,319
- I’ll call you.
- Uh...

460
00:32:15,720 --> 00:32:16,720
Where are you?

461
00:32:20,240 --> 00:32:23,240
Tony, when Ryan skips class, where does he usually go?

462
00:32:26,119 --> 00:32:28,400
Okay. Can you send Teach your location?

463
00:32:28,799 --> 00:32:29,799
Thanks.

464
00:32:39,039 --> 00:32:40,039
Ryan.

465
00:33:19,240 --> 00:33:20,519
Ow...

466
00:33:21,240 --> 00:33:24,799
You’re this bad? Just go home and slide the worm.

467
00:33:38,400 --> 00:33:41,680
Mm... gotcha now, Ryan.

468
00:33:42,680 --> 00:33:44,480
Go home and come back to Teach nicely.

469
00:33:44,839 --> 00:33:47,559
Your mom’s really worried right now, you know that?

470
00:33:54,279 --> 00:33:55,279
Ryan.

471
00:33:55,640 --> 00:33:57,119
Come home with Teach.

472
00:33:57,640 --> 00:34:00,439
Okay? You can play games anytime. Your mom’s worried.

473
00:34:00,440 --> 00:34:03,279
No. Ryan wants to play. Teach, stay out of it.

474
00:34:15,480 --> 00:34:17,000
Then let’s play.

475
00:34:18,000 --> 00:34:20,719
If Teach loses,

476
00:34:21,000 --> 00:34:23,400
I’ll leave quietly and go home.

477
00:34:24,400 --> 00:34:26,239
But if Ryan loses

478
00:34:27,119 --> 00:34:28,719
you’re coming home with me.

479
00:34:29,320 --> 00:34:30,320
Deal?

480
00:34:31,639 --> 00:34:34,840
I don’t go easy on chickens, Teach.

481
00:34:35,159 --> 00:34:37,400
Losing to a kid would be embarrassing, Teach.

482
00:34:42,719 --> 00:34:45,639
Come and get me.

483
00:34:55,440 --> 00:34:56,840
Hey, don’t run.

484
00:35:04,079 --> 00:35:05,519
If you’ve got guts, come ou.

485
00:35:05,679 --> 00:35:07,280
Ow hey.

486
00:35:07,960 --> 00:35:09,920
Help.

487
00:35:12,960 --> 00:35:14,400
Hiyah

488
00:35:14,719 --> 00:35:16,159
Ryan wants a rematch.

489
00:35:18,280 --> 00:35:19,280
A rematch.

490
00:35:21,360 --> 00:35:23,079
Ryan’s serious now.

491
00:35:26,159 --> 00:35:27,199
One more time.

492
00:35:30,199 --> 00:35:32,039
Rematch, please. Rematch. Rematc.

493
00:35:35,000 --> 00:35:36,480
Gun Slinger God.

494
00:35:54,360 --> 00:35:55,639
Hiyah.

495
00:36:01,760 --> 00:36:05,119
Teach... are you the real Tep G.

496
00:36:06,639 --> 00:36:10,158
I’m gonna tell everyone. I met the real Tep G.

497
00:36:10,159 --> 00:36:11,800
No way.

498
00:36:13,039 --> 00:36:15,000
This stays between us.

499
00:36:18,599 --> 00:36:20,039
- Don’t tell anyone.
- Ryan.

500
00:36:21,280 --> 00:36:23,199
Do you know how worried your aunt and mom were?

501
00:36:24,400 --> 00:36:25,599
Ryan.

502
00:36:26,679 --> 00:36:27,999
Your mom was worried, sweetheart.

503
00:36:28,119 --> 00:36:29,799
Why did you go off without telling anyone?

504
00:36:30,079 --> 00:36:31,480
I already told you.

505
00:36:31,639 --> 00:36:32,936
When did you tell us, sweetheart?

506
00:36:32,960 --> 00:36:34,919
Back then, at that time.

507
00:36:34,920 --> 00:36:37,598
Oh, and when exactly was ‘back then, at that time’?

508
00:36:37,599 --> 00:36:39,559
Back then, at that time.

509
00:36:39,800 --> 00:36:41,320
Sweetheart...

510
00:36:59,159 --> 00:37:00,599
Tep G.

511
00:37:01,039 --> 00:37:02,039
What?

512
00:37:02,440 --> 00:37:03,559
Do you know Tep G?

513
00:37:04,360 --> 00:37:05,760
Ryan told me

514
00:37:06,039 --> 00:37:08,880
he got to play a game with Tep G, his idol.

515
00:37:09,400 --> 00:37:11,239
Oh, Tep G?

516
00:37:11,639 --> 00:37:14,519
Yeah. Really good at games

517
00:37:15,639 --> 00:37:17,280
Ryan totally idolizes Tep G.

518
00:37:17,639 --> 00:37:19,400
So who’s better you or Tep G?

519
00:37:20,000 --> 00:37:23,760
Tep G, obviously, P’Pee. How could Kao even compare?

520
00:37:24,519 --> 00:37:26,119
But I do wonder...

521
00:37:26,280 --> 00:37:28,639
what is it about gaming

522
00:37:29,079 --> 00:37:30,960
that people enjoy so much, huh?

523
00:37:32,599 --> 00:37:33,960
I’ll tell you.

524
00:37:34,639 --> 00:37:36,440
For other people,

525
00:37:38,039 --> 00:37:39,800
games are like basketball is for you, P’Pee.

526
00:37:41,119 --> 00:37:42,320
It’s fun.

527
00:37:43,239 --> 00:37:44,559
It’s a dream.

528
00:37:47,119 --> 00:37:48,360
But in your family,

529
00:37:48,880 --> 00:37:50,760
games were never something happy, were they?

530
00:38:02,440 --> 00:38:05,239
So it was because P’Phan ran away from home, right?

531
